## 4. What happens in each stop/failure case

### 4.1 Heavy worker stops

Expected behavior:

```text
Gateway remains online.
Telegram/WhatsApp session remains connected.
Incoming messages can still be received.
Gateway can wake a new worker when needed.
```

This is the most important efficiency goal.

### 4.2 Gateway process stops gracefully

Expected behavior:

```text
Live replies stop.
Session files remain in gateway state dir.
Gateway can restart and reconnect.
Control plane marks gateway offline/reconnecting.
```

Need ensure shutdown flushes:

```text
journal
outbox
checkpoints
personal runtime state
```

### 4.3 Gateway crashes

Expected behavior:

```text
Heartbeat becomes stale.
Control plane marks gateway stale/offline.
System service restarts gateway.
Gateway reloads local state.
Gateway reconnects.
Personal channel runtime starts again.
```

### 4.4 VPS/container restarts

Expected behavior:

```text
Live replies pause during restart.
Persistent volume survives.
Gateway loads same state.
Session should restore.
```

### 4.5 VPS/container destroyed but volume survives

Expected behavior:

```text
Replacement container can attach same volume.
Gateway identity/session state may recover.
Control plane may require recovery confirmation if host/device identity changed.
```

### 4.6 VPS/container and volume destroyed

Expected behavior:

```text
Session is lost in gateway-local mode.
User reconnects Telegram/WhatsApp.
```

Do not lie about this.

### 4.7 Session vault exists later

Expected behavior:

```text
Gateway downloads encrypted session blob.
Cloud lease prevents duplicates.
Gateway restores session.
Live operation resumes.
```

This is future, not MVP.

