## 5. Product modes

### 5.1 Local Customer Hardware Gateway

User runs Agent Computer on their own Mac/Windows/Linux machine.

Best for:

```text
local files
local apps
desktop control
private personal channels
maximum trust
power users
```

Pros:

```text
strongest privacy story
personal sessions remain on user-owned hardware
matches current trust-boundary docs
```

Cons:

```text
user machine must be awake/online
onboarding is harder
not reliable for always-on customer support unless the user machine is stable
```

### 5.2 User-Provided VPS / Self-Hosted Agent Computer

User provides a VPS and connects it through SSH/pairing.

Important security truth:

```text
If the user owns the VPS, the user can inspect it.
You cannot hide all runtime internals from the root owner of the machine.
```

Do not put platform master secrets on user-owned hardware.

Only put:

```text
workspace-scoped gateway token
short-lived session token
runtime-specific local state
supervisor local secret
user's own personal channel session material
```

Never put:

```text
global signing keys
platform provider master secrets
other tenants' data
billing secrets
admin credentials
cloud database credentials
```

### 5.3 Company-Provided Hosted VPS / Hosted Agent Computer

Empyralis provides the VPS/container.

The user should not receive SSH/root access. They see only:

```text
status
connect/reconnect flows
logs after redaction
channel health
cost/usage
start/stop/revoke buttons
```

Best for:

```text
normal users
customer support automation
hosted personal Telegram
hosted WhatsApp with dedicated container
business pilots
```

Pros:

```text
better UX
always-on possible
company controls security baseline
users do not configure servers
```

Cons:

```text
Empyralis now stores/hosts sensitive personal channel sessions
more security responsibility
more cost
more legal/privacy responsibility
```

### 5.4 On-Demand Hosted Gateway

Only starts when user asks.

Good for:

```text
cheap users
manual tasks
"check my Telegram now"
proof of concept
```

Bad for:

```text
24/7 customer support
real-time replies
instant inbound automation
```

### 5.5 Always-On Lightweight Gateway

Gateway stays online; heavy agent sleeps.

This is the key efficient business model.

Flow:

```text
Gateway stays online.
Inbound message arrives.
Gateway publishes event to control plane.
Control plane wakes worker.
Worker decides/drafts/sends.
Gateway sends reply.
Worker sleeps.
Gateway remains online.
```

This is how you avoid paying for a full AI computer per user 24/7.

### 5.6 Dedicated Hosted Gateway Container

Each workspace gets a dedicated gateway container/volume.

Use this for:

```text
WhatsApp personal
Signal
browser-profile channels
high-value business users
```

Do not mix multiple customers' personal channel sessions in one messy shared filesystem. That is not architecture. That is evidence.

