## 7. Channel-specific recommendation

### 7.1 Telegram Personal: launch first

Why:

```text
Telegram session restore is more realistic.
The repo already has Telegram personal runtime and session store.
Session string is stored under gateway state root.
Telegram is more forgiving than WhatsApp.
Good demonstration of the gateway advantage.
```

MVP behavior:

```text
User opens Agent Computer > Personal Channels > Telegram.
User enters Telegram setup details / code / 2FA as current UI supports.
Gateway stores session under persistent gateway state dir.
Gateway reports connected state.
Incoming messages wake Sage/agent worker.
Worker replies through gateway.
Worker can sleep without killing gateway.
Gateway restart restores session.
```

### 7.2 WhatsApp Personal: second, dedicated gateway/container

Why not first:

```text
WhatsApp Web/Baileys sessions are fragile.
QR/pairing state can expire.
IP/device changes can trigger re-login.
Duplicate sessions can break behavior.
```

MVP behavior:

```text
Use dedicated hosted gateway/container.
Persist whatsapp/auth under gateway state dir.
Show QR/pairing/needs-login state clearly.
Do not promise cross-machine failover at first.
```

### 7.3 WhatsApp Business API: separate business lane

Use official WhatsApp Business API for business agents where possible.

This belongs to:

```text
Studio / deployed-agent / business connector lane
```

Not the same as personal WhatsApp gateway.

### 7.4 Signal / iMessage / WeChat: not launch first

Treat as bridge/planned/private runtime until real tests prove:

```text
real account setup
durable replay
outbound approval
health reporting
account lifecycle
session restore
```

### 7.5 Gmail / Email

Prefer OAuth/API connector, not browser login, when possible.

